    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n      \"title\": \"肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\",\n      \"purpose\": \"综合不同实体瘤中微生物特征（多样性、特定菌属、代谢物）与临床结局（ORR、PFS、OS）的观察性关联数据，明确抗生素等药物暴露的负面影响，并区分早期干预性试验信号与确证性证据的界限。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、HCC、CRC 等实体瘤的 ICI 治疗队列。纳入观察性队列研究、荟萃分析及 I/II 期干预性试验的临床结局数据。排除血液系统恶性肿瘤、无微生物组数据的纯临床研究及纯动物机制研究。\",\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0404\",\n          \"reason\": \"甲状腺癌 ICI 疗效系统综述，未涉及肠道微生物组数据，无法支持本章微生物关联论点。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0492\",\n          \"reason\": \"犬癌症免疫治疗微生物组研究，物种差异大，不能直接作为人类实体瘤临床证据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0256\",\n          \"reason\": \"TNBC ICI 治疗现状综述，未包含微生物组与疗效关联的具体数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0508\",\n          \"reason\": \"抗生素对 I 期试验生存影响研究，核心结果缺失，无法提取有效效应量。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0549\",\n          \"reason\": \"仅摘要且为概念性综述，缺乏具体临床关联数据支持本章实证论述。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0009\",\n          \"reason\": \"侧重分子机制（肌苷-UBA6），临床数据仅为 CheckMate 025 分层，主要归入 Ch3 机制章节。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0114\",\n          \"reason\": \"机制研究摘要，缺乏独立临床队列关联数据，主要归入 Ch3。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"thread_id\": \"T1_Taxa_Consistency\",\n          \"thesis\": \"特定菌属（Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium）在黑色素瘤、NSCLC 和 RCC 中 consistently 与 ICI 疗效正相关，但效应大小受肿瘤类型和地理人群修饰。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0014\",\n            \"P0033\",\n            \"P0298\",\n            \"P0495\",\n            \"P0545\",\n            \"P0565\"\n          ],\n          \"argumentative_role\": \"确立微生物组作为预测因子的生物学合理性基础，同时通过反例（如 P0270, P0301）说明非普适性。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_id\": \"T2_Functional_Diversity\",\n          \"thesis\": \"高α多样性及治疗期间微生物组稳定性与更长 PFS/OS 相关，功能通路（如 SCFA 合成）比单一分类学特征更具跨队列预测潜力。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0092\",\n            \"P0104\",\n            \"P0200\",\n            \"P0227\",\n            \"P0354\",\n            \"P0496\"\n          ],\n          \"argumentative_role\": \"从分类学关联向功能/生态特征深化，解释为何单一菌种标志物在不同研究中不一致。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_id\": \"T3_Pharmacological_Modulators\",\n          \"thesis\": \"抗生素暴露（特别是 ICI 启动前 30-60 天内）显著降低 OS 和 PFS，PPI 使用亦有负面影响，但效应受肿瘤类型（如 HCC vs NSCLC）和抗生素种类修饰。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0039\",\n            \"P0052\",\n            \"P0068\",\n            \"P0575\",\n            \"P0576\",\n            \"P0275\"\n          ],\n          \"argumentative_role\": \"提供药物 - 微生物 - 免疫轴的临床流行病学证据，强调临床管理中避免不必要的菌群扰动。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_id\": \"T4_Interventional_Signals\",\n          \"thesis\": \"FMT 联合 ICI 在 I/II 期试验（MIMic, FMT-LUMINate, TACITO）中显示 ORR 和 PFS 改善信号，但 MITRIC 试验阴性结果及缺乏 III 期 RCT 表明其尚未成为标准疗法。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0577\",\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0586\",\n            \"P0578\",\n            \"P0590\",\n            \"P0591\"\n          ],\n          \"argumentative_role\": \"区分观察性关联与干预性证据，明确当前证据等级为早期探索性，避免过度解读为确证性疗效。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"ordered_themes\": [\n        {\n          \"theme_title\": \"特定菌属与临床结局的观察性关联\",\n          \"content_focus\": \"报告 Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium 在黑色素瘤 (P0033, P0565)、NSCLC (P0104, P0182)、RCC (P0495) 中的正相关数据；对比 HCC (P0301) 和 mCRPC (P0270) 中的阴性或矛盾结果，论证肿瘤类型特异性。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0014\",\n            \"P0033\",\n            \"P0104\",\n            \"P0270\",\n            \"P0298\",\n            \"P0301\",\n            \"P0495\",\n            \"P0545\",\n            \"P0565\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme_title\": \"微生物多样性、稳定性与功能通路\",\n          \"content_focus\": \"分析α多样性与预后的关系（P0104, P0200）；引入纵向稳定性概念（P0033, P0227）；讨论 SCFA 合成等功能通路比物种丰度更具预测力（P0092, P0496）。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0033\",\n            \"P0092\",\n            \"P0104\",\n            \"P0200\",\n            \"P0227\",\n            \"P0354\",\n            \"P0496\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme_title\": \"抗生素与 PPI 暴露的负面影响\",\n          \"content_focus\": \"汇总抗生素使用时机（P0052, P0575）、时长（P0061）及种类对 OS/PFS 的荟萃分析数据；讨论 PPI 的独立影响（P0135, P0339）及 HCC 中的例外情况（P0275）。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0039\",\n            \"P0052\",\n            \"P0061\",\n            \"P0068\",\n            \"P0135\",\n            \"P0275\",\n            \"P0339\",\n            \"P0575\",\n            \"P0576\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme_title\": \"干预性试验的临床信号与局限\",\n          \"content_focus\": \"报告 FMT 联合 ICI 的 Phase 1/2 结果（MIMic ORR 65%, FMT-LUMINate ORR 70%, TACITO PFS 改善）；对比 MITRIC 阴性结果（ORR 0%）；强调缺乏 III 期 RCT 及安全性顾虑（P0583 毒性 65%）。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0577\",\n            \"P0578\",\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0586\",\n            \"P0590\",\n            \"P0591\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_paper_synthesis\": [\n        {\n          \"synthesis_point\": \"菌属效应的肿瘤特异性\",\n          \"description\": \"综合 P0014 (NSCLC/RCC), P0033 (Melanoma), P0495 (RCC) 显示 Akkermansia 的普遍正相关，但需结合 P0270 (mCRPC) 和 P0301 (HCC) 的阴性结果，论证微生物标志物不能脱离肿瘤微环境背景泛化。\",\n          \"supporting_sources\": [\n            \"P0014\",\n            \"P0033\",\n            \"P0270\",\n            \"P0301\",\n            \"P0495\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"synthesis_point\": \"抗生素效应的时机依赖性\",\n          \"description\": \"整合 P0052 (NSCLC Meta), P0575 (Timing), P0061 (Duration) 数据，确立 ICI 启动前 30-60 天为关键风险窗，且效应量在 NSCLC 中较黑色素瘤更稳健（P0547）。\",\n          \"supporting_sources\": [\n            \"P0052\",\n            \"P0061\",\n            \"P0547\",\n            \"P0575\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"synthesis_point\": \"FMT 疗效的异质性\",\n          \"description\": \"对比 P0577 (MIMic 阳性), P0583 (LUMINate 阳性), P0586 (TACITO 中性) 与 P0578 (MITRIC 阴性)，指出供体筛选、预处理方案及患者基线免疫状态（如髓系优势）是决定干预成败的关键变量。\",\n          \"supporting_sources\": [\n            \"P0577\",\n            \"P0578\",\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0586\",\n            \"P0590\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"conditions_and_limitations\": [\n        {\n          \"condition\": \"研究设计类型\",\n          \"detail\": \"明确区分观察性队列（如 P0014, P0033）与干预性试验（如 P0577, P0583）。观察性数据仅报告关联（HR, OR），不得暗示因果；干预性数据需标注分期（Phase 1/2 vs 3）及对照设置（单臂 vs RCT）。\",\n          \"impact\": \"防止将早期 FMT 信号误读为确证性疗效，避免将观察性关联误读为因果机制。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"condition\": \"样本量与统计效力\",\n          \"detail\": \"标注小样本研究（如 P0104 n=70, P0495 n=31, P0578 n=15）的局限性，其结果视为探索性信号。荟萃分析（P0052, P0068）需报告异质性（I²）及发表偏倚风险。\",\n          \"impact\": \"避免过度泛化小队列发现，保持对统计不确定性的诚实报告。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"condition\": \"肿瘤类型与治疗背景\",\n          \"detail\": \"严格限定结论适用的癌种（如 P0585 仅限 NSCLC 化疗 - 免疫联合，P0545 仅限波兰黑色素瘤）。不将单一癌种结论（如黑色素瘤 FMT）直接外推至所有实体瘤。\",\n          \"impact\": \"确保临床建议的精准性，反映微生物 - 免疫互作的情境依赖性。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"condition\": \"混杂因素控制\",\n          \"detail\": \"报告各研究对饮食、抗生素、PPI、地理因素的校正情况。未校正混杂因素的研究（如部分 P0301）其结论需谨慎引用。\",\n          \"impact\": \"提高证据的可信度，解释不同研究间结果不一致的潜在原因。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"transition_logic\": \"本章确立了微生物组与 ICI 疗效在临床层面的广泛关联及药物干扰证据，但观察性数据无法解释‘如何’介导。这将自然过渡到 Ch3，深入解析特定代谢物（如肌苷、SCFA）及免疫细胞互作的具体分子机制，同时 Ch3 将明确区分动物模型机制与人类临床验证的界限。\",\n      \"supplement_requests\": [],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n          \"focus\": \"提取 NSCLC 化疗 - 免疫联合背景下产丁酸菌与 OS 关联的具体 HR 值及不同免疫方案（NIC vs PC）的差异数据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n          \"focus\": \"确认 FMT-LUMINate 试验中 NSCLC 与黑色素瘤队列的 ORR 具体数值及 3-4 级不良事件发生率，特别是双药 ICI 背景下的毒性信号。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0298\",\n          \"focus\": \"获取 NSCLC 和黑色素瘤中微生物特征与生存/响应改善的定量荟萃效应量，用于支撑关联的一致性论述。\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": []\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants a chapter proposal for \"Ch2_Clinical\" of a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\nThe chapter title is \"肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\" (Clinical Association Evidence between Gut Microbiome and ICI Efficacy).\nThe purpose is to synthesize observational data on microbial features (diversity, specific taxa) and clinical outcomes (survival, response) across different solid tumors, distinguishing observational from interventional evidence.\nKey tasks include reporting specific taxa (Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium) associated with positive outcomes, analyzing antibiotic exposure data, presenting heterogeneity across tumor types (Melanoma, NSCLC, RCC), and distinguishing correlation from causation.\n\nI need to structure the chapter proposal with:\n1.  **Chapter ID & Title**: As provided.\n2.  **Purpose**: Refined based on the routing and shared outline.\n3.  **Scope**: Boundaries of evidence (observational vs interventional, tumor types).\n4.  **Substantive Threads**: The main argumentative lines within the chapter.\n5.  **Ordered Themes**: How the content flows.\n6.  **Concrete Cases/Comparisons**: Specific studies to cite (using source handles).\n7.  **Cross-Paper Synthesis**: How to combine findings without overgeneralizing.\n8.  **Conditions and Limitations**: Crucial for maintaining accuracy (e.g., sample size, study design).\n9.  **Transition Logic**: How this chapter leads to the next (Mechanisms).\n10. **Supplement Requests**: If there are gaps needing further search (though the prompt says limited supplementary search found no matches, I should check if any specific gaps remain based on the routing).\n11. **Directed Reads**: Specific sources to focus on.\n12. **Excluded Source Handles**: If any routed sources are truly out of scope (should be minimal).\n13. **Screened Sources**: Sources deemed not useful with reasons.\n\nI have a large list of routed sources (P0002 to P0591). I need to select the most relevant ones for *Clinical Association Evidence* (Ch2).\nKey sources for Ch2 from the routing list include:\n-   P0014 (Routy et al., Science 2018 - Akkermansia, Antibiotics)\n-   P0033 (Longitudinal changes in Melanoma)\n-   P0092 (SCFAs in Solid Tumors)\n-   P0298 (Meta-analysis NSCLC/Melanoma)\n-   P0543 (Review on leveraging microbiota)\n-   P0585 (JCOG2007 ancillary - NSCLC Chemo-immuno)\n-   P0583 (FMT-LUMINate - Interventional but provides clinical outcome data)\n-   P0586 (TACITO - Interventional)\n-   P0039 (Meta-analysis on Antibiotics/Probiotics/FMT)\n-   P0052 (Meta-analysis on Antibiotics in NSCLC)\n-   P0068 (Meta-analysis on Antibiotics)\n-   P0104 (NSCLC specific)\n-   P0121 (HCC specific)\n-   P0148 (KRAS-mutated NSCLC)\n-   P0182 (Japanese NSCLC cohort)\n-   P0200 (NSCLC integrative stratification)\n-   P0270 (mCRPC - negative/contradictory example)\n-   P0301 (HCC - negative example)\n-   P0327 (NSCLC - negative example)\n-   P0495 (mRCC)\n-   P0545 (Polish Melanoma - population specific)\n-   P0565 (Systematic Review Melanoma)\n-   P0575 (Antibiotic Timing)\n-   P0577 (MIMic FMT Phase 1)\n-   P0578/0590 (MITRIC FMT - negative)\n-   P0591 (FMT-LUMINate Abstract)\n\nI need to organize these into themes:\n1.  **Taxonomic Associations**: Specific genera (Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium) across tumors.\n2.  **Functional/Metabolic Associations**: SCFAs, diversity, stability.\n3.  **Negative Modulators**: Antibiotics, PPIs, timing.\n4.  **Heterogeneity**: Tumor type (Melanoma vs NSCLC vs RCC vs HCC), Geography, Treatment regimen.\n5.  **Interventional Signals**: FMT trials (MIMic, TACITO, MITRIC, FMT-LUMINate) - distinguishing Phase 1/2 signals from lack of Phase 3.\n\nI must ensure I don't overclaim causality for observational studies.\nI need to check the `unresolved_limits` from the input:\n-   Large scale RCT results (unmet) -> Ch2 must label interventional evidence as early phase.\n-   Specific metabolite quantification (partial) -> Ch2 should report stratification data (e.g., CheckMate 025 inosine) but note lack of absolute concentration.\n-   Directed read unavailable (8016df...) -> Do not claim to have this data.\n\nI will draft the chapter proposal in JSON format.\nI need to make sure I don't just list sources but explain *how* they will be used to build the argument.\nI need to identify `excluded_source_handles` if any routed sources are not suitable for Ch2 (e.g., pure mechanism papers without clinical data, or blood cancer papers).\nLooking at the routing, many sources are reviews or mechanism-heavy. I should filter for those providing *clinical association evidence*.\nSources like P0009, P0114 (pure mechanism abstracts) might be better for Ch3.\nSources like P0404 (Thyroid cancer systematic review) might be excluded if no microbiome data.\nSources like P0492 (Dogs) should be excluded.\nSources like P0256 (TNBC ICI utilization without microbiome) should be excluded.\n\nLet's refine the source list for Ch2.\nIncluded: P0014, P0033, P0039, P0052, P0068, P0092, P0104, P0121, P0148, P0182, P0200, P0270, P0298, P0301, P0327, P0495, P0543, P0545, P0565, P0575, P0577, P0578, P0583, P0585, P0586, P0590, P0591.\nExcluded (for Ch2, maybe better for Ch3/Ch5/Ch6 or out of scope): P0009 (Mechanism), P0114 (Mechanism abstract), P0404 (No microbiome), P0492 (Dogs), P0256 (No microbiome), P0272 (Excluded in principles), P0404 (Thyroid, no microbiome).\nActually, the instruction says \"Do not silently drop a routed source... name it in excluded_source_handles\".\nI will check the routed list provided in the input. There are many. I will select the most relevant for Ch2 and exclude those that are purely mechanistic (for Ch3) or purely interventional methodology (for Ch5) or out of scope (blood cancer, no microbiome).\nHowever, many reviews cover both. I will keep reviews that summarize clinical associations in Ch2.\nI will exclude sources that are explicitly about blood cancer (e.g., P0539 focuses on hematologic, though mentions solid, might be borderline. Better to exclude if solid tumor data is minor).\nI will exclude P0404 (Thyroid, no microbiome).\nI will exclude P0492 (Dogs).\nI will exclude P0256 (TNBC, no microbiome).\nI will exclude P0508 (Results missing).\nI will exclude P0549 (Abstract only, very limited).\n\nLet's structure the `substantive_threads`.\n1.  **Consistency of Taxonomic Signals**: Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium across Melanoma, NSCLC, RCC.\n2.  **Diversity and Stability**: Alpha diversity, longitudinal stability vs baseline.\n3.  **Pharmacological Modulators**: Antibiotics (timing, class), PPIs.\n4.  **Contextual Heterogeneity**: Tumor type, Geography, Regimen (Chemo-immuno vs ICI alone).\n5.  **Interventional Clinical Signals**: FMT trials (ORR, PFS signals vs lack of Phase 3).\n\nI need to ensure the `interpretation_limits` from the routing are respected (e.g., observational vs causal, sample size).\n\nLet's write the JSON.",
